   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the insurance law and the public health law, in relation to\nadverse determinations related to a step therapy protocol override\ndetermination; and to repeal certain provisions of the insurance law and the\npublic health law relating thereto",
    "basePrintNo": "S8038",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8038-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Rpld §4902 sub§ (a) ¶14, §4903 sub§ (e-1), amd §§4902 & 4903, Ins L; rpld §4902 sub 1 ¶(1), §4903 sub 5-a, amd §§4902 & 4903, Pub Health L (as proposed in S.2677-A & A.463-A)",
    "lawSection": "Insurance Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8038\n\nSPONSOR: BRESLIN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the insurance law and the public health law, in relation\nto adverse determinations related to a step therapy protocol override\ndetermination; and to repeal certain provisions of the insurance law and\nthe public health law relating thereto\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2023,\nc.735, to require notice of adverse step therapy determinations.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation requires insurers to share additional information with\nconsumers when delivering notices of adverse step therapy determinations\nand allows electronic delivery of such notices.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter Amendment to Chapter 735 of the Laws of 2023. 5.2677A and A.463A\nboth passed the Senate and Assembly in June 2023.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nChapter of the Laws of 2023 amending the Insurance Law and the Public\nHealth La relating to requiring notice of adverse step therapy determi-\nnations, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.2677-A and A.463-A,\ntakes effect.\n",
